  "blocks": {
    "\"Look at the ticket graph — the schema change blocks the backfill, the backfill blocks the API switch. Pick a leaf and run a session on it.\"": "“查看任务图——schema 变更会阻塞回填，回填又会阻塞 API 切换。选一个叶节点，在其上启动一次会话。”",
    "\"Where do I start on the migration spec?\"": "“从迁移规格说明的哪里开始？”",
    "A good ticket is written for a reader with no other context. The goal, the acceptance criteria, and context pointers to the relevant files and decisions — enough that the session can start working without re-deriving what the last one knew.": "优秀任务的读者不应需要其他上下文。它需要包含目标、验收标准，以及指向相关文件和决策的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-pointer\">上下文指针</a>——足以让会话直接开始工作，而不用重新推导上一会话已经掌握的内容。",
    "A handoff artifact scoping one session of work. Stands alone, or hangs off a spec as one of its children. Tickets can block or be blocked by sibling tickets, so the order of work falls out of their dependency graph rather than a linear plan.": "任务是一份限定单次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>工作范围的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/handoff-artifact\">交接产物</a>。它可以独立存在，也可以作为<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/spec\">规格说明</a>的子项挂在其下。任务之间可能相互阻塞，因此工作顺序应由依赖图推导，而不是由线性计划决定。",
    "The defining constraint is the size: one session. A ticket should be completable before the session drifts out of the smart zone — and that constraint is testable. If sessions on your tickets routinely degrade before the work is done, the tickets are too big; split them. If each session spends most of its context on setup before doing five minutes of work, they're too small; merge them.": "任务的定义性约束是规模：一次会话。任务应当在会话离开<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/smart-zone\">聪明区</a>前完成，而且这一约束可以验证。如果执行任务的会话经常在工作完成前发生退化，说明任务太大，应拆分；如果每次会话在真正工作五分钟之前，大部分上下文都耗在准备上，说明任务太小，应合并。",
    "The dependency graph is also what unlocks parallelism. Independent tickets — the leaves of the graph — can each run in their own session at the same time. This is an effective way of running multiple agents at once.": "依赖图还会解锁并行执行。互相独立的任务——依赖图的叶节点——可以同时在各自会话中运行。这是并行运行多个智能体的有效方式。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
